================================================================================
Path to commercial use
================================================================================

You have these options for using Splattie commercially:

1. Use only the widget + format. Generate `.splattie` files through your own
   pipeline. The widget loads any `.splattie` that follows the spec - it does
   not require LAM or FLAME at runtime.

2. License FLAME and/or SMPL-X commercially with MPI for Intelligent Systems
   when using the reference head or body generators. The rest of the stack is
   Apache 2.0 / MIT.

3. Use the object generator path when FLAME / SMPL-X are not needed. TRELLIS,
   Puppeteer, gsplat, Three.js, and Spark are MIT / Apache 2.0.

4. Implement an alternative generation method behind the `AssetGenerationMethod`
   protocol (see backend/src/splattie/methods/). Bring your own
   commercially-licensed reconstruction model and rig. The rest of the stack
   stays the same.

The `.splattie` format itself is method-agnostic. `manifest.json.generator.method`
declares which method produced the file; the widget does not care.
